## 🏗️ Architecture

```
                    ┌───────────────────────────┐
                    │   React SPA (Tailwind)    │
                    └─────────────┬─────────────┘
                                  │ HTTPS (JSON + httpOnly refresh cookie)
                    ┌─────────────▼─────────────┐
                    │  Nginx (reverse proxy)    │  TLS · serves React build · proxies /api
                    └─────────────┬─────────────┘
                                  │
        ┌─────────────────────────▼─────────────────────────┐
        │        API process — Express modular monolith     │
        │                                                   │
        │  auth · companies · employees · departments ·     │
        │  leave · attendance · notifications · reports ·   │
        │  audit                                            │
        │                                                   │
        │  Routes → Controllers → Services → Repositories   │
        └──────┬──────────────────────────────┬─────────────┘
               │ SQL (transactions, locks)    │ cache · rate limits ·
               │                              │ reset tokens
        ┌──────▼───────────┐           ┌──────▼──────┐
        │   PostgreSQL     │           │    Redis    │
        │ business tables  │           └─────────────┘
        │ + outbox_events  │
        └──────┬───────────┘
               │ polled (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)
        ┌──────▼───────────┐   publish   ┌─────────────────────┐
        │  Outbox relay    ├────────────►│       Kafka         │
        │  (worker)        │             │ leave-events        │
        └──────────────────┘             │ employee-events     │
                                         │ attendance-events   │
                                         │ *.dlt               │
                                         └──────────┬──────────┘
                              ┌─────────────────────┴─────────────────────┐
                    ┌─────────▼──────────┐                      ┌─────────▼──────────┐
                    │ Notification worker│                      │  Reporting worker  │
                    │ group: notifications│                     │ group: reporting   │
                    │ in-app + email     │                      │ monthly aggregates │
                    └────────────────────┘                      └────────────────────┘
```

**One codebase, multiple processes.** The API and workers share the same modules but run as separate Node processes (`src/server.js`, `src/workers/*.js`). This is still a monolith — one repo, one database, one deployable — but slow side effects (email) can never block an API request.

### Request layering

| Layer | Responsibility | Must NOT |
|---|---|---|
| **Routes** | URL + HTTP method → middleware chain → controller | contain logic |
| **Controllers** | Read validated input, call a service, shape the HTTP response | contain business rules or SQL |
| **Services** | Business rules, transactions, authorisation decisions, audit + outbox writes | know about `req`/`res` |
| **Repositories** | Parameterised SQL; every function takes `companyId` | contain business rules |
| **Database** | Constraints, locks, RLS — the last line of defence | — |

### Synchronous vs asynchronous

| Operation | Mechanism | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| Approve leave + deduct balance | **One DB transaction** | Must be atomic |
| Prevent overlapping leave | **DB exclusion constraint** | Only the DB sees all concurrent inserts |
| Audit log | **Same DB transaction** as the change | An audit trail that can lose entries is useless |
| Check-in / check-out | **Synchronous** | User needs immediate confirmation |
| Email & in-app notifications | **Outbox → Kafka → worker** | Slow, retryable, user doesn't wait |
| Monthly statistics | **Outbox → Kafka → worker** | Derived data; eventual consistency is fine |

