## 🧭 Key Design Decisions

> ⚠️ **Pending confirmation.** Decisions 1–6 below use the mentor's recommended defaults and should be confirmed (or changed) before implementation. Update this table once agreed.

| # | Decision | Chosen (recommended) | Alternative considered |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Tenant isolation | Shared schema + `company_id` + composite FKs + **Postgres RLS** | App-level `WHERE` only; schema-per-tenant; DB-per-tenant |
| 2 | Event publishing | **Transactional outbox** | Publish after commit (can lose events); Debezium CDC (heavy) |
| 3 | Identity | Email **globally unique**; one user belongs to one company | Email unique per company (login then needs company selection) |
| 4 | Approvals | Reporting manager approves; HR/admin can approve anyone (incl. people with no manager) | Manager-only; multi-level approval chains |
| 5 | Leave rules | Mon–Fri working days (no public holidays yet), half days allowed, yearly up-front allocation, **pending days reserved**, carry-forward up to policy limit | Monthly accrual; holiday calendar; no reservation |
| 6 | Attendance | One check-in + one check-out per day; one start time + grace period per company | Multiple sessions/day; per-employee shifts |
| 7 | DB access | **`pg` (node-postgres) + raw SQL**, migrations via `node-pg-migrate` | ORM (Prisma/Sequelize) — hides the locking/transactions this project is meant to show |
| 8 | Validation | **Zod** | Joi (equally fine) |
| 9 | IDs | UUID (`gen_random_uuid()`) | bigserial — guessable, enables ID enumeration |
| 10 | Architecture | **Modular monolith** + separate worker processes | Microservices — no genuine reason at this scale |

