## 🔧 Environment Variables

```env
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=4000
CLIENT_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# PostgreSQL — app role (no table ownership, subject to RLS)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://worksphere_app:app_password@localhost:5432/worksphere
# PostgreSQL — migration/owner role (used only by migrations)
MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://worksphere_owner:owner_password@localhost:5432/worksphere
DB_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS=5000

REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

KAFKA_BROKERS=localhost:9092
KAFKA_CLIENT_ID=worksphere

JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=change-me-long-random
JWT_ACCESS_TTL=15m
REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL_DAYS=7
BCRYPT_ROUNDS=12

PASSWORD_RESET_TTL_SECONDS=900
APP_URL=http://localhost:5173

SMTP_HOST=localhost
SMTP_PORT=1025
MAIL_FROM="WorkSphere <no-reply@worksphere.test>"

LOG_LEVEL=info
REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
```

All variables are validated at startup by `config/env.js`; the process exits with a clear message if any are missing or malformed.

